+Proposed outcome/exit acceptance matrix (P2-TRUST; reasons remain in retained evidence):
+
+| Observation after an admitted verification attempt | `provenancePolicy` / `artifactBinding` | Requested policy result; exit with otherwise complete analysis |
+|---|---|---|
+| Exact subject, valid crypto, all explicit expectations met | `verified_policy` / `matched` | `pass`; 0. This establishes the stated policy only. |
+| Exact subject and valid crypto, no policy selected | `verified_cryptographic_only` / `matched` | `not_evaluated`; 0. No policy acceptance or safety claim. |
+| Exact subject and valid crypto, supported explicit identity/source/builder expectation fails | `verified_cryptographic_only` / `matched` | `violation`; 1, with the failed expectation. Keep crypto success separate from policy rejection. |
+| Invalid signature/chain/log binding, or authenticated statement for wrong subject digest/package/version | `invalid` / `matched`, `mismatched` or `not_available` as actually established | 1 only when the selected supported policy defines this as a violation; otherwise indeterminate/2. A subject name mismatch is recorded even if its digest matches. No policy: `not_evaluated`; incomplete verification produces 2. |
